		Held to 40rem and centred, which is the fix for "why is this so big". It
		had no measure at all: `.growth__wide` runs to 90rem and this filled it, so
		on a wide window the clip was over 1400px across — larger than the two
		screenshots that carry the actual proof, and larger than the widest source
		the poster ever offered, so it was upscaled as well as oversized.

		A talking head does not need width. It needs to be legible and to sit under
		the argument it supports.
	*/
	.film {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.9rem;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 40rem;
		margin-block-start: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
